\section{Sensitivity to the background}
\label{app:background}
The value function is marginal with $B=50$ random training rows throughout.
Figure~\ref{fig:background} changes the background to $B=20$ or $B=200$ random rows or to $50$ $k$-means centroids for the \texttt{shap} Kernel explainer on German Credit ($9$--$20$ instances) and ACS Employment ($30$), at the reference budget; each background has its own exact reference.
The exact top-3 set itself differs from the one under $B=50$ for most instances ($B=20$: the same for $0.23$--$0.47$; $B=200$: $0.46$--$0.89$; $k$-means: $0.50$--$0.89$), so the reference moves toward stability as $B$ grows without settling by $B=200$.
The single run's tolerance-aware correctness is unchanged under every background (all paired differences are exactly zero), and its strict correctness changes by at most $0.09$ with intervals that mostly include zero.
This is a statement about a subset of the instances; the data for the remaining instances and for the floor of two independent backgrounds at each $B$ were not available.

